<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kingdom of Strathclyde</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">5th–11th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> · Also known as Alt Clut, Kingdom of Alt Clut</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kingdom of Strathclyde was a Brittonic kingdom of the early medieval north, centred first on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dumbarton-rock">Dumbarton Rock</a>, called Alt Clut, and after a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> siege of 870 on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/govan">Govan</a> and the Clyde valley. Its kings fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaels">Gaels</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dal-riata">Dál Riata</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/picts">Picts</a> and the Northumbrians. In the 11th century it was absorbed into the kingdom of the Scots.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-strathclyde.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Strathclyde" width="320" height="316" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hogweard · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_the_Kingdom_of_Strathclyde_9-10th_century_en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Domnall Brecc joined Congal Cáech of the Ulaid in his war against the Irish high king and was defeated at the Battle of Mag Rath in 637, which weakened Dál Riata’s position in Ireland; he was killed fighting the <b>Britons of Strathclyde</b> at Strathcarron in 642.</blockquote><a href="/empire/dal-riata">Dal Riata · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>He styled himself king of the English, and in 937 he defeated a coalition of Scots, <b>Strathclyde Britons</b> and Dublin Vikings at the Battle of Brunanburh.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-england">Kingdom of England · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Eadberht (737–758) took Kyle in Ayrshire and in 756, with the Pictish king Óengus, forced the <b>Britons of Dumbarton</b> to submit, but lost most of his army shortly afterwards.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-northumbria">Kingdom of Northumbria · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>In the early Middle Ages the Picts fought the Gaels of Dál Riata, the <b>Britons of Alt Clut</b> (Dumbarton) and the Angles of Northumbria.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-picts">Kingdom of the Picts · Military</a></li></ul></section>
